Z||000000||jd2m4||12-09-2001||08:31 PM||||I found a 2.8 v-6 out of a chevy corisca. I was going to modify it pretty much the same way i modded the small-block chevy in my 82 firebird.The block would be bored .30 over,And i would be useing flat-top pistons,the crank would be turned .10 under,Magnaflux the connecting rods to make sure they're o.k.,Double roller timeing chain,roller rockers,Crane compu cam (264/274 adevertised duration,423/423gross lift),Shave the heads,Do a 3-angle valve job,port and polish them,Port and polish the intake,Performance plugs and wires (thinking about accell)Port the exaust manifolds,Power pullys,and free flowing exaust,160 degree thermostat.I was hopeing to wind up with a engine putting out at least 200 horsepower.What do you guys think?Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
